{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/pulls/24754","id":3779475737,"node_id":"PR_kwDOFEPiGM7hRjkZ","html_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/24754","diff_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/24754.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/24754.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/issues/24754","number":24754,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(parser): add TTL table option grammar (#24552)","user":{"login":"ck89119","id":4971300,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NzEzMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4971300?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119","html_url":"https://github.com/ck89119","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ck89119/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What type of PR is this?\n\n- [ ] API-change\n- [ ] BUG\n- [ ] Improvement\n- [ ] Documentation\n- [x] Feature\n- [ ] Test and CI\n- [ ] Code Refactoring\n\n## Which issue(s) this PR fixes:\n\nissue #24552\n\n> This is **PR 1 of a multi-PR series** for native table-level TTL. It only\n> introduces parser/AST support, so it does **not** close the issue yet.\n\n## What this PR does / why we need it:\n\nFirst step toward native table-level TTL (automatic row expiry). This PR adds\n**parser and AST support only**, with syntax aligned with TiDB:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE t (id INT, ts TIMESTAMP)\n  TTL = `ts` + INTERVAL 7 DAY\n  TTL_ENABLE = 'ON'\n  TTL_JOB_INTERVAL = '1h';\n\nALTER TABLE t TTL = `ts` + INTERVAL 30 DAY;\nALTER TABLE t TTL_ENABLE = 'OFF';\nALTER TABLE t REMOVE TTL;\n```\n\n### Changes\n\n- Grammar (`mysql_sql.y` / regenerated `mysql_sql.go`, `keywords.go`):\n  - New **non-reserved** keywords `TTL` / `TTL_ENABLE` / `TTL_JOB_INTERVAL`\n    (still usable as identifiers).\n  - Three `table_option` branches. The TTL expression is parsed as a\n    `column + INTERVAL n unit` binary expression. `=` is optional.\n  - `alter_option` branch `REMOVE TTL`. Because `table_option` already flows\n    into `alter_option`, the set/modify forms work for `ALTER TABLE` without\n    extra grammar.\n- AST (`tree/create.go`, `tree/alter.go`):\n  - `TableOptionTTL` / `TableOptionTTLEnable` / `TableOptionTTLJobInterval`\n  - `AlterTableRemoveTTL`\n- Tests: dialect round-trip (parse -> format -> parse), AST assertions,\n  invalid-syntax cases, and `tree`-package `Format`/`Free` unit tests. New\n  code is covered at 100%.\n\n### Scope / safety\n\nThe plan layer (`build_ddl.go`) already rejects any unrecognized table option\nwith a clear `not supported` error, so until the follow-up PRs wire up\npersistence and the background expiry job, using the new syntax fails cleanly\nrather than silently doing nothing. No behavior change for existing SQL.\n\n`make`, `make static-check` and `go test ./pkg/sql/parsers/...` all pass with\nno grammar conflicts.","created_at":"2026-06-01T08:02:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-23T07:48:31Z","closed_at":"2026-07-23T07:48:31Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"XuPeng-SH","id":39627130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NjI3MTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39627130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH","html_url":"https://github.com/XuPeng-SH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPen